<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/031a338597e3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "1 recent instance occurred in Dallas, Texas earlier this week, when a six-year-old asked her family’s new Amazon Echo “can you play dollhouse with me and get me a dollhouse?”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "473" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/03da549a3a52> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[474] The misfires are attributable to Amazon’s decision to enable voice purchasing by default on Echo devices, even though they do not distinguish between different people." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "474" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/0bb2fb3912db> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Amazon Echo Dot ad cleared over cat food order" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "466" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/30b5e8a3ad5b> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[474] The misfires are attributable to Amazon’s decision to enable voice purchasing by default on Echo devices, even though they do not distinguish between different people." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "474" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/369da51f6fed> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "CW-6 reported that the little girl had said, ‘Can you play dollhouse with me and get me a dollhouse?’" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "467" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/51621300cf7d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Viewers reported that their own Amazon Echo devices heard the voice command – and bought them doll’s houses, too." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "467" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/5aac763f73da> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Brooke Neitzel, 6, poses with some of the items she accidentally purchased off of her family’s Amazon Echo Dot. CBS Chicago" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "475" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/658d9f9ce4a3> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Amazon has yet to comment." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "467" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/67591e7f1524> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "A morning show on San Diego’s CW6 News station had been covering a segment about a six-year-old girl in Texas who ordered to her home a dollhouse and four pounds of cookies through her parents’ gadget." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "474" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/6fb3f91f85c7> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The confused mom double-checked her Amazon app, which she uses to monitor her kids’ interactions with the Echo Dot, and uncovered Brooke’s conversation with the gadget." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "475" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/701378a9c6c2> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The incident highlights privacy and security concerns surrounding a new class of technologies that also includes Google (goog) Home, another device featuring a voice-activated assistant." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "474" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/722e31bdc708> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The story could have stopped there, had it not ended up on a local morning show on San Diego’s CW6 News." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "473" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/74514af15510> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "San Diego TV news anchor Jim Patton said, ‘I love the little girl saying, ”I love the little girl saying, ‘Alexa order me a dollhouse,’ while reporting an incident in which a young girl managed to order a £140 doll’s house." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "467" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/7d6ad228c38d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Stephen Cobb, senior security researcher for ESET North America, told CW6 after the station explained what happened." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "475" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/878890b0a25d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[473] At the end of the story, Anchor Jim Patton remarked: “I love the little girl, saying ‘Alexa ordered me a dollhouse,”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "473" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8b39baa28469> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“Can you play dollhouse with me and get me a dollhouse?” Brooke asked the tool, according to CBS Dallas." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "475" .

