<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ab53c0a65a7c> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Amazon’s Alexa started ordering people dollhouses after hearing its name on TV" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "473" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/b542b49bf05d> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Amazon Echo's Alexa Went Dollhouse Crazy" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "474" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/bc22fa073a40> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Owners complained that their voice-activated devices set off on an inadvertent shopping spree after a California news program triggered the systems to make erroneous purchases, according a local report." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "474" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c0240ee89534> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[466] The devices overheard a television news anchor on CW6 in San Diego talking about a child who managed to order a doll's house and a tin of cookies from Alexa because the family had not activated parental controls on their Echo device." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "466" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c50ae9eea956> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[474] Owners complained that their voice-activated devices set off on an inadvertent shopping spree after a California news program triggered the systems to make erroneous purchases, according a local report." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "474" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c7b2f3959f53> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "“A handful” of people said that their devices accidentally tried to buy the toys, reported the Verge, which spoke to the station, although the total figure is not known." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "474" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/c9579d12408a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Patton didn’t think that any of the devices went through with their purchases, who told The Verge that the station received a handful of reports of viewer devices attempting to order a dollhouse after hearing his remarks." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "473" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ed41e1a9c3b0> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Echo devices, powered by Amazon (amzn) Alexa, the tech giant’s artificially intelligent voice assistant, reportedly woke when they heard the name “Alexa” spoken on household television sets." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "474" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/fff902a57eb9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[474] The misfires are attributable to Amazon’s decision to enable voice purchasing by default on Echo devices, even though they do not distinguish between different people." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "474" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/Risk/513b1d5a15f2> a airo:Risk ;
    rdfs:label "risk of unintended or erroneous AI-initiated purchases from voice commands" ;
    airo:confidenceScore "0.95"^^xsd:float ;
