<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/2e544f6128be> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[474] A “handful” of people said that their devices accidentally tried to buy the toys, reported the Verge, which spoke to the station, although the total figure is not known." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "474" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/43415cf07335> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Amazon clarified to CBS News that there was not an influx of dollhouse orders after the newscast." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "475" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/8a5ed37d5d9e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "After reading the conversation, Neitzel had to laugh, admitting that this was a good reminder to activate parental controls and turn off voice purchasing." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "475" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/ce0a9dbc4b2e> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[474] Owners complained that their voice-activated devices set off on an inadvertent shopping spree after a California news program triggered the systems to make erroneous purchases, according a local report." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "474" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/db8b177c3a47> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "[474] The incident highlights privacy and security concerns surrounding a new class of technologies that also includes Google (goog) Home, another device featuring a voice-activated assistant." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "474" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f913c9e02603> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The device readily complied, ordering a KidKraft Sparkle mansion dollhouse, in addition to “four pounds of sugar cookies.”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "473" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/155cc3a61869> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "You must ask Alexa to order a product and then confirm the purchase with a “yes” response to purchase via voice." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "475" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/3fe258dae479> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "At the end of the story, Anchor Jim Patton remarked: “I love the little girl, saying ‘Alexa ordered me a dollhouse,”" ;
    airo:sourceDocId "473" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/41ea9eb37fcd> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Amazon’s new Echo device is programmed to respond to voice commands whenever it hears the word, ‘Alexa’ – and this can lead to disaster." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "467" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/f8d5f469d91a> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The advert, which aired in October, featured a man asking Amazon's voice assistant Alexa to order Purina cat food." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "466" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/72e3f5c970d9> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "The Advertising Standards Authority (ASA) announced that it would not uphold the consumer's complaint because it did not find the advert to be in breach of the UK Code of Broadcast Advertising." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "466" .

<https://w3id.org/airo/incident/evidence/a0cab54b5148> a airo:Evidence ;
    airo:evidenceText "Dallas mom Megan Neitzel’s cautionary tale involving her 6-year-old daughter accidentally ordering pricey gifts through “Alexa,” Amazon’s voice-activated Echo Dot, went viral last week." ;
    airo:sourceDocId "475" .

